{
 "about": "Trade kits: what a person of a trade is expected to carry, wear and keep at home, the food in their house, and what they would never own (docs/design/items.md, section People and households; skill place-stock). A person takes the first kit whose `match` (a pattern over their trade, case-insensitive) or `roles` (person_role) fits, then every overlay whose `races` fits (a Dunmer or Imperial household's own goods). A household's store follows its head's kit. `carry`, `wear` and `home` are expectations the stocker draws from (a slot, a weapon type or armour slot keyword, the materials of ours in order of preference, and a good for wares); `never` rows are what `stock reach` reports as a contradiction when a person's possessions or their household's store hold one: every condition a row names must hold (slot, type keyword, materials, groups, bands). A stock row with an `exception` (its reason in words) is never reported. Nothing here is a roll (decision 0035). Read by tools/newworld/stockdb.py (trade_kit, trade_kit_item, trade_kit_never) and tools/places/stock/reach.py.",
